---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import TaskTreeDemo from '../../components/TaskTreeDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Task Tree" description="A live list of tasks drawn as a tree, with a status mark on each.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Task Tree</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows the tasks of a run and how they break into parts. A task with one part continues straight down; a task with
    several branches them out. Each row has a Status mark, so the tree updates as your app changes task states. For a
    saved plan with criteria and dependencies, use Plan Outline. For agents that start other agents, use Agent Fanout.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <TaskTreeDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Task Tree usage"
      code={`import { TaskTree } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/task-tree";

<TaskTree
  tasks={[
    {
      id: "scaffold",
      title: "Scaffolding project",
      state: "success",
      children: [
        { id: "deps", title: "Installing dependencies", state: "running", value: 40, detail: "40%" },
        { id: "ignore", title: "Ignoring DB files", state: "success", children: [
          { id: "readme", title: "Writing README", state: "pending" },
        ] },
      ],
    },
  ]}
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>tasks</code>: <code>{'{ id, title, state?, value?, detail?, children? }'}</code>. <code>state</code> and{' '}
        <code>value</code> go to Status. <code>detail</code> is short muted text at the end of the row, such as a
        duration or a count.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>children</code>: the task's parts. One part stays in the same column with a straight line. Two or more
        move one column in, each with its own branch.
      </li>
      <li>
        A task with parts and no <code>state</code> follows them: failed if any part failed, running if any is running,
        succeeded once all have finished. While running, its ring fills with the share of parts done. Set{' '}
        <code>state</code> to override it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>title</code>: the heading, “Tasks” by default. <code>summary</code> replaces the “3 of 8 done” count; pass{' '}
        <code>null</code> to hide it. The count covers tasks without parts. Succeeded, warning, and skipped tasks count
        as done.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>empty</code>: shown when there are no tasks. Defaults to “No tasks yet.”
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Lines are drawn with React Flow at a fixed 24px column and 32px row, with panning, zoom, and selection turned off.
      Long titles end in an ellipsis.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Motion</h2>
    <p>
      When a task succeeds, a green line grows from it up to its parent over 280ms. A parent that follows its parts
      changes only once that line arrives, so the green climbs the tree one level at a time. Other changes show at once.
      Rows added later fade in over 220ms. The server sends a static drawing of the same tree, which React Flow replaces
      in place without replaying anything. With reduced motion, lines turn green at once and rows only fade.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The section is named by its heading. Screen readers get the tasks as nested lists, with each Status mark named
      after its state, such as “Running, 40%”; the drawing is hidden from them. The done count is a polite live region,
      so progress is announced as tasks finish.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Lines use <code>--sprout-muted</code> mixed 40% into <code>--sprout-surface</code>, and{' '}
      <code>--sprout-success</code> once the task below them has succeeded. Pending and skipped titles use{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>. In forced colors, lines use <code>GrayText</code> and finished lines{' '}
      <code>CanvasText</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
